# Copy to `.env` and fill in. `.env` is git-ignored.
# The e2e/api/hybrid suites run fine WITHOUT any of these — only the AI layer
# (aiExpect assertions + CI failure summaries) needs Claude credentials.
#
# Pick ONE credential source:

# (a) API key — simplest, and what CI uses (GitHub secret ANTHROPIC_API_KEY).
#     Get one at https://console.anthropic.com
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=

# (b) OAuth bearer token — if you authenticate via OAuth (e.g. `ant auth login`).
#     Export a short-lived token; the client adds the required oauth beta header.
#       eval "$(ant auth print-credentials --env)"      # sets ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN
#     or paste one here (it expires, so prefer the eval form):
# ANTHROPIC_AUTH_TOKEN=

# (c) On-disk profile — if the SDK can resolve an `ant auth login` profile from
#     disk, set this flag to force-enable the AI features (bare `new Anthropic()`).
#     NOTE: the standalone test process does NOT share Claude Code's login, so
#     this only works if you've run `ant auth login` separately.
# AI_ENABLED=1

# Optional overrides
# BASE_URL=https://www.automationexercise.com
# AI_MODEL=claude-opus-4-8
# AI_EFFORT=low
